  "notes": [
    "Irregular -AR verb with an *e→ie* stem change (same pattern as *pensar*, *cerrar*, *sentar*): the stressed *e* becomes *ie* everywhere except nosotros/nosotras and the Pretérito Indefinido/Imperfecto/Futuro/Condicional, which stay fully regular",
    "Past participle: *acertado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to guess right\" or \"to get something right\" — *acerté la respuesta* (I got the answer right), *acertó el número de la lotería* (he/she guessed the lottery number correctly)",
    "Also used with *a* + infinitive meaning \"to happen to\" or \"to manage to\": *acertó a encontrar la salida* (he/she managed to find the exit)",
    "Related: *acierto* (a correct guess, a good decision — noun), *desacertar* (to get it wrong — less common opposite), *acertado/a* (apt, well-chosen)"
  ],
